1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,341
[car door opens]

2
00:00:07,466 --> 00:00:09,217
[distant barking]

3
00:00:09,218 --> 00:00:11,261
[birds chirping]

4
00:00:13,472 --> 00:00:16,224
[engine revs]

5
00:00:16,225 --> 00:00:17,559
[sighs]

6
00:00:19,061 --> 00:00:21,480
[dramatic music playing]

7
00:00:41,542 --> 00:00:43,377
[tires screeching]

8
00:00:45,587 --> 00:00:47,338
[music intensifies]

9
00:00:47,339 --> 00:00:48,506
[engine revving]

10
00:00:48,507 --> 00:00:50,383
[tires screeching]

11
00:00:50,384 --> 00:00:51,552
[car horn honks]

12
00:00:51,677 --> 00:00:52,678
Chou Chin-lai!

13
00:00:53,095 --> 00:00:54,179
Pull over!

14
00:00:55,639 --> 00:00:58,684
[tires screeching]

15
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:04,231
Pull over! Hey!

16
00:01:04,565 --> 00:01:06,358
[car horn honks]

17
00:01:07,484 --> 00:01:09,443
Pull over! Pull over!

18
00:01:09,444 --> 00:01:10,696
[tires screeching]

19
00:01:12,406 --> 00:01:13,532
Son of a bitch!

20
00:01:24,126 --> 00:01:26,336
[engine revving]

21
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:30,215
[tires screeching]

22
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:32,134
[crash]

23
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:43,228
[crickets chirping]

24
00:01:59,536 --> 00:02:01,204
[car door opens]

25
00:02:03,165 --> 00:02:04,291
[door closes]

26
00:02:11,465 --> 00:02:13,300
[distant barking]

27
00:02:18,764 --> 00:02:20,474
[mumbles]

28
00:02:21,767 --> 00:02:24,353
[chuckles]

29
00:02:26,730 --> 00:02:28,732
No, it's impossible.

30
00:02:29,691 --> 00:02:30,651
No way!

31
00:02:30,776 --> 00:02:34,112
Damn! Freaking bastard!

32
00:02:34,237 --> 00:02:37,282
Son of a bitch! [screams]

33
00:02:37,407 --> 00:02:38,784
Freaking bastard!

34
00:02:39,201 --> 00:02:40,327
Damn!

35
00:02:40,452 --> 00:02:42,454
[pants]

36
00:02:44,373 --> 00:02:46,583
[dramatic music playing]

37
00:03:01,306 --> 00:03:02,641
[retching and coughing]

38
00:03:05,811 --> 00:03:08,230
[engine whirring]

39
00:03:14,611 --> 00:03:15,696
[car door opens]

40
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:17,989
[door closes]

41
00:03:27,541 --> 00:03:29,417
Wen.

42
00:03:29,418 --> 00:03:32,754
Wen, I didn't do it on purpose.
I didn't do it on purpose.

43
00:03:37,634 --> 00:03:38,677
[Wen] It's alright,
it's alright.

44
00:03:38,885 --> 00:03:40,511
- But...
- It's alright.

45
00:03:40,512 --> 00:03:41,679
But I killed somebody.

46
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:43,724
It's alright! Okay?

47
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:46,435
You're fine.

48
00:03:47,436 --> 00:03:50,564
Drive home now.

49
00:03:50,731 --> 00:03:52,524
Leave it to me.

50
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:13,754
[door closes]

51
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:15,547
Why are you home now?

52
00:04:26,516 --> 00:04:27,768
Well,

53
00:04:29,686 --> 00:04:30,854
I'm wondering...

54
00:04:33,857 --> 00:04:36,442
if we settle
with Chou Lu-yung now,

55
00:04:36,443 --> 00:04:37,569
is it too late?

56
00:04:40,614 --> 00:04:41,740
Chien-yuan,

57
00:04:43,742 --> 00:04:45,702
do you know
what a settlement means?

58
00:04:49,748 --> 00:04:52,751
It means you drove the car.

59
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:56,671
You're the successor
to Chang Xin.

60
00:04:57,756 --> 00:04:59,507
A successor
with a criminal record.

61
00:04:59,508 --> 00:05:01,927
Do you think
this is good for you?

62
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:03,595
[suspenseful music playing]

63
00:05:04,596 --> 00:05:06,306
Hmm?

64
00:05:13,647 --> 00:05:17,316
Feeling guilty
won't help you grow.

65
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:18,443
Understand?

66
00:05:26,618 --> 00:05:27,828
Here.

67
00:05:27,953 --> 00:05:29,663
Taste the pork.
See if it's good.

68
00:05:39,798 --> 00:05:41,424
[laughs]

69
00:05:41,967 --> 00:05:43,759
[sighs]

70
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:50,559
We're not allowed
to eat dog meat,
but we eat pork every day.

71
00:05:52,435 --> 00:05:57,899
What's interesting is that pigs
are more intelligent than dogs.

72
00:05:59,609 --> 00:06:04,948
But even if most people
know that fact,
we'll keep eating pork.

73
00:06:06,116 --> 00:06:07,492
Do you know why?

74
00:06:12,414 --> 00:06:14,833
Because every part
of the pig is delicious.

75
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:18,461
Nobody protects pigs.

76
00:06:19,671 --> 00:06:21,673
Like Chin-lai and his son.

77
00:06:22,966 --> 00:06:25,718
People like them
are born to be eaten,

78
00:06:25,719 --> 00:06:28,846
so you don't need
to feel guilty for them.

79
00:06:28,847 --> 00:06:30,015
Understand?

80
00:06:37,981 --> 00:06:41,568
[singer] <i>♪ Someday, you can
Find sunshine, sunshine ♪</i>

81
00:06:41,818 --> 00:06:46,364
[singing in Mandarin]

82
00:06:46,489 --> 00:06:48,699
<i>♪ Run, run, to hope ♪</i>

83
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:50,784
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

84
00:06:50,785 --> 00:06:52,870
<i>♪ I believe in you someday ♪</i>

85
00:06:52,871 --> 00:06:54,915
[singing in Mandarin]

86
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:58,919
<i>♪ Someone just like you
Lights up my dream ♪</i>

87
00:06:59,044 --> 00:07:01,838
[singing in Mandarin]

88
00:07:08,553 --> 00:07:10,055
I'm so glad
you're joining the competition.

89
00:07:10,472 --> 00:07:12,015
It'll be so exciting.

90
00:07:13,892 --> 00:07:16,436
So, who else is competing?

91
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:19,730
Everyone I asked
was willing to join.

92
00:07:19,731 --> 00:07:23,068
The chefs from these restaurants
deserve to be known by everyone.

93
00:07:25,654 --> 00:07:26,738
But Chieh?

94
00:07:27,739 --> 00:07:29,824
Jin Lai Hao is a food truck.

95
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:34,662
You know them?
They're great. Their dishes
are very sophisticated.

96
00:07:34,663 --> 00:07:36,664
They used to have a storefront,

97
00:07:36,665 --> 00:07:38,916
but that has nothing to do
with their cooking skills, right?

98
00:07:38,917 --> 00:07:40,584
Yeah, I know them.

99
00:07:40,585 --> 00:07:42,462
But in that case, Chang Xin
might not be able to join.

100
00:07:45,715 --> 00:07:47,759
It brings down our class
to compete with a food truck.

101
00:07:52,555 --> 00:07:55,683
They're very popular
on the Internet.

102
00:07:55,684 --> 00:07:58,895
I know chefs
from traditional restaurants
might be more skilled,

103
00:07:59,062 --> 00:08:02,983
but those young people
are better at online marketing.

104
00:08:03,191 --> 00:08:05,776
So, other restaurants
have no objections?

105
00:08:05,777 --> 00:08:07,112
No.

106
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:10,656
Jin Lai Hao is so popular online
that these other restaurants

107
00:08:10,657 --> 00:08:12,074
want to jump on the bandwagon
to transform themselves.

108
00:08:12,075 --> 00:08:13,910
If we work together,
it'll be a win-win situation.

109
00:08:14,119 --> 00:08:16,996
Chang Xin represents
quality Taiwanese cuisine.

110
00:08:16,997 --> 00:08:19,457
We'll try our best
to make it known with the show.

111
00:08:19,582 --> 00:08:20,959
Why don't you think it over?

112
00:08:23,545 --> 00:08:25,672
I'm sorry, Chieh,
but it's really not appropriate.

113
00:08:28,967 --> 00:08:30,093
[Chien-yuan] Wait.

114
00:08:32,721 --> 00:08:33,805
Hsiu-wen?

115
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:41,479
Actually,
it won't bring down our class.

116
00:08:41,604 --> 00:08:45,733
The show is really popular.
Besides, we have the best chefs.

117
00:08:45,734 --> 00:08:46,818
Don't worry.

118
00:08:47,986 --> 00:08:50,030
Fine. It's up to you.

119
00:08:50,155 --> 00:08:51,865
I'm only telling you
what I think.

120
00:08:54,868 --> 00:08:56,619
- Chieh?
- Eh?

121
00:08:59,706 --> 00:09:01,833
[upbeat music playing]

122
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,711
TAIWANESE CUISINE SHOWDOWN
THE BATTLE OF REBORN CLASSICS

123
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:13,928
[narrator] <i>Ladies and gentlemen,
this week's</i> Super Chef
<i>is packed.</i>

124
00:09:14,095 --> 00:09:16,181
<i>Online sensation
Jin Lai Hao Food Truck</i>

125
00:09:16,306 --> 00:09:18,891
<i>versus second-generation
Wu Wei She,</i>

126
00:09:18,892 --> 00:09:21,186
<i>fighting for a spot
in the next round
with Taiwanese fusion.</i>

127
00:09:21,561 --> 00:09:24,689
<i>It's bound to be
a furious battle,
and incredibly exciting.</i>

128
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:27,941
<i>Without further ado,
let's get started!</i>

129
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:30,195
<i>You have one hour.</i>

130
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:32,112
- Let's go!
- [bell ringing]

131
00:09:32,113 --> 00:09:35,033
Marinate the duck legs first,
then cut the pork blood cake.

132
00:09:35,241 --> 00:09:36,618
CHOU LU-YUNG AND MA YU-LI,
JIN LAI HAO

133
00:09:36,868 --> 00:09:37,869
Go, Jin Lai Hao!

134
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:39,913
You're a super chef, Boss!

135
00:09:41,039 --> 00:09:44,833
Green Bamboo Shoot Salad
with Lemon-caper Vinaigrette.

136
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:47,087
German Pork Knuckle
with Salted Egg Yolk.
It sounds delicious.

137
00:09:47,212 --> 00:09:48,588
It must be Ailanthus Prickly
Ash Quiche.

138
00:09:48,713 --> 00:09:50,047
<i>I'm so looking forward to it.</i>

139
00:09:50,048 --> 00:09:51,883
- What are you making?
- A hamburger.

140
00:09:52,884 --> 00:09:55,095
[host] <i>It's actually
a Steamed Minced Beef
with Pickles Hamburger.</i>

141
00:09:55,303 --> 00:09:58,765
<i>We've all guessed wrong.
What's the matter?</i>

142
00:09:58,890 --> 00:10:00,225
[Lu-yung]
I'll marinate the duck legs.

143
00:10:00,642 --> 00:10:02,810
After that, cut the pork blood
cake into small pieces.

144
00:10:02,811 --> 00:10:03,895
[Lu-yung] Okay.

145
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:06,939
[host] Looks like
they're a great team.

146
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:10,067
Jin Lai Hao, what kind of dish
are you going to present today?

147
00:10:10,068 --> 00:10:11,986
- You'll see.
- [host] Cool!

148
00:10:12,237 --> 00:10:15,907
You're trying
to give us a surprise.
Let's wait and see.

149
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:19,119
French-style...

150
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:21,621
- Milkfish Donburi.
- Braised Pork Cake!

151
00:10:21,746 --> 00:10:23,248
Taco Fried Rice, maybe.

152
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:25,083
[interviewer] <i>Okay, let me
tell you their ingredients,</i>

153
00:10:25,208 --> 00:10:27,127
<i>and you guess
what they're making, okay?</i>

154
00:10:27,252 --> 00:10:30,796
<i>They've got mullet roe,
duck legs,</i>

155
00:10:30,797 --> 00:10:33,049
<i>pork blood cake,
brown sugar bun cakes,
and white radish.</i>

156
00:10:33,216 --> 00:10:35,009
<i>What do you think?</i>

157
00:10:35,176 --> 00:10:36,261
How do these ingredients
go together?

158
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:38,012
It's a Truth or Dare
punishment, isn't it?

159
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:39,264
A Lunar New Year market.

160
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:41,808
My background
is in Western cuisine.

161
00:10:41,933 --> 00:10:44,768
<i>I've always wanted
to try fusion cuisine.</i>

162
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:47,188
<i>I know these ingredients
look weird.</i>

163
00:10:47,397 --> 00:10:51,317
But trust me,
we're going to create a dish
that touches your heart.

164
00:10:51,943 --> 00:10:53,861
<i>Yu-li is bold with her choice
of ingredients.</i>

165
00:10:53,862 --> 00:10:56,781
<i>But she actually
has a secret.</i>

166
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:58,032
In fact, I'm afraid of fire.

167
00:10:58,199 --> 00:10:59,659
It's shocking, right?

168
00:10:59,784 --> 00:11:01,161
<i>I used to get bullied.</i>

169
00:11:01,286 --> 00:11:04,831
<i>Back then, someone tried
to burn my hair,</i>

170
00:11:04,956 --> 00:11:07,167
<i>which left me
with some major demons.</i>

171
00:11:07,292 --> 00:11:09,002
<i>But I can't be defeated
like that.</i>

172
00:11:09,169 --> 00:11:10,420
<i>I've been in the kitchen...</i>

173
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:13,797
Getting bullied?
Fishing for sympathy?

174
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:16,009
Chao Yi-hsuan
must've taught her that.

175
00:11:16,176 --> 00:11:18,845
When you want to cry,
chop up some onions.

176
00:11:18,970 --> 00:11:20,263
[imitates chopping]

177
00:11:21,764 --> 00:11:23,724
I think she's cute.

178
00:11:23,725 --> 00:11:25,267
She's acting.

179
00:11:25,268 --> 00:11:27,269
<i>I'd like to thank
my co-workers
at Jin Lai Hao.</i>

180
00:11:27,270 --> 00:11:29,314
<i>They've been
my biggest strength,
supporting me.</i>

181
00:11:29,731 --> 00:11:31,149
<i>As long
as you keep holding on...</i>

182
00:11:31,274 --> 00:11:33,233
- [Chien-yuan]
She looks familiar.
<i>- and never give up,</i>

183
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:35,320
<i>you can definitely
overcome your fears.</i>

184
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:37,822
[host] <i>Okay, guys. Counting down
the final seconds.</i>

185
00:11:37,947 --> 00:11:40,992
<i>Our contestants are putting
on the finishing touches.</i>

186
00:11:41,117 --> 00:11:45,914
<i>Are they going to serve up
creative surprises
or upgraded classics?</i>

187
00:11:47,332 --> 00:11:49,124
[host] <i>Wu Wei She has made</i>

188
00:11:49,125 --> 00:11:51,044
<i>a Steamed Beef with Pickles
Hamburger with Salted Pork.</i>

189
00:11:51,169 --> 00:11:53,004
<i>The minced beef infused
with the aromatic pickles</i>

190
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:57,090
<i>challenges our judges'
taste buds to the limit.</i>

191
00:11:57,091 --> 00:11:58,718
Is that edible?

192
00:12:01,179 --> 00:12:03,723
[host] <i>The dishes
from Jin Lai Hao
have long names.</i>

193
00:12:03,848 --> 00:12:05,225
<i>I'll just give you
the last one.</i>

194
00:12:05,350 --> 00:12:07,685
<i>And for dessert, Brown Sugar
Bun Cakes and Mochi.</i>

195
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:10,229
<i>The names already
sound incredible.
They went all out.</i>

196
00:12:10,230 --> 00:12:12,940
<i>You're going to eat
to your heart's content.</i>

197
00:12:12,941 --> 00:12:15,025
They're not creative at all.
We're bound to win.

198
00:12:15,026 --> 00:12:16,194
Go, Jin Lai Hao!

199
00:12:17,737 --> 00:12:20,113
[host] <i>All judges
are savoring the dishes.</i>

200
00:12:20,114 --> 00:12:22,825
<i>What will the results be?</i>

201
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:27,080
Okay. Here are the results.
[laughs]

202
00:12:27,205 --> 00:12:29,249
The judges have racked
their brains.

203
00:12:29,457 --> 00:12:31,709
It's been a battle
of the taste buds.

204
00:12:31,834 --> 00:12:33,044
Let's start
with Wu Wei She's hamburger.

205
00:12:33,211 --> 00:12:35,088
The aroma is off the charts.

206
00:12:35,213 --> 00:12:37,340
<i>You'll be impressed
by the mind-blowing
creativity.</i>

207
00:12:37,757 --> 00:12:40,342
<i>Next is Jin Lai Hao's
Ginger Duck Combo.</i>

208
00:12:40,343 --> 00:12:43,179
It's so rich that
it's like savoring a symphony
of Taiwanese cuisine.

209
00:12:43,388 --> 00:12:46,181
It's absolute perfection.

210
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:47,934
Both teams are pulling out
all of their tricks.

211
00:12:48,059 --> 00:12:49,560
It's a clash of titans.

212
00:12:51,479 --> 00:12:55,400
Who will get the ticket
to the final?

213
00:12:55,775 --> 00:12:57,317
<i>Congratulations to...</i>

214
00:12:57,318 --> 00:12:59,069
Jin Lai Hao!

215
00:12:59,070 --> 00:13:00,405
[crowd cheering]

216
00:13:00,822 --> 00:13:02,365
[upbeat rock music playing]

217
00:13:03,241 --> 00:13:05,326
Jin Lai Hao is number one!

218
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:13,960
Good job!

219
00:13:14,085 --> 00:13:15,169
[scoffs]

220
00:13:16,087 --> 00:13:17,171
Damn!

221
00:13:21,968 --> 00:13:24,095
Boss, you look good in that cap.

222
00:13:27,015 --> 00:13:28,766
[host] <i>Congratulations,
Jin Lai Hao! They are through
to the final.</i>

223
00:13:28,891 --> 00:13:31,101
<i>Next week, Yi Gong
Restaurant will compete</i>

224
00:13:31,102 --> 00:13:33,771
<i>against the unbeatable king
of Taiwanese cuisine,
Chang Xin.</i>

225
00:13:33,896 --> 00:13:36,106
<i>From Chang Xin,
Stephen Cheng...</i>

226
00:13:36,107 --> 00:13:41,028
I'm grateful to all
of our regulars who truly love
Chang Xin's dishes.

227
00:13:41,029 --> 00:13:42,113
[host] <i>...and Annie Lo.</i>

228
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:43,989
I have an absolute passion
for cooking.

229
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:45,241
And I know I'm talented.

230
00:13:45,450 --> 00:13:49,161
Along the way as a chef,
I've never struggled.

231
00:13:49,162 --> 00:13:51,163
[host] <i>Who will win
this competition?</i>

232
00:13:51,164 --> 00:13:52,998
<i>What's more exciting is,</i>

233
00:13:52,999 --> 00:13:54,959
<i>the voting for Favorite Chef
has already begun.</i>

234
00:13:55,084 --> 00:13:58,212
<i>Every single vote could
decide who wins or loses!</i>

235
00:13:58,379 --> 00:14:00,465
[birds chirping]

236
00:14:01,299 --> 00:14:02,425
Excuse us.

237
00:14:08,181 --> 00:14:10,307
- Hi, Yu-li.
- Hi, Wen.

238
00:14:10,308 --> 00:14:12,060
- Here to visit your granny?
- Yeah.

239
00:14:14,395 --> 00:14:17,273
[laughs] Oh, I put on
new makeup for him.

240
00:14:18,149 --> 00:14:19,484
You did a good job.

241
00:14:19,901 --> 00:14:21,234
[Wen] He loves it...

242
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:22,487
I think.

243
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:25,990
I can see you love
your son very much.

244
00:14:29,202 --> 00:14:30,411
Why are you always here alone?

245
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:31,954
Where are your parents?

246
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:35,375
I only have my dad,

247
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:37,417
but he was always
being transferred
from place to place.

248
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:40,087
I was brought up by my granny.

249
00:14:40,088 --> 00:14:43,007
My granny bought me
my first dress.

250
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:46,677
It seems your family
supports you.

251
00:14:50,139 --> 00:14:52,100
Only my granny is nice to me.

252
00:14:52,433 --> 00:14:56,186
My dad is in the military
and cannot accept it at all.

253
00:14:56,187 --> 00:14:59,190
We haven't seen
each other for many years.

254
00:14:59,357 --> 00:15:02,359
Not everyone has a good father
like Yu-chih does.

255
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:04,529
[emotional music playing]

256
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:06,989
I'm not a good father.

257
00:15:07,490 --> 00:15:09,409
It wasn't until
after the accident...

258
00:15:10,535 --> 00:15:12,537
that it made me rethink things.

259
00:15:16,124 --> 00:15:19,544
Wen, didn't you tell me Yu-chih
wanted to move to Thailand

260
00:15:20,336 --> 00:15:24,048
because trans women there
can be movie stars
and you wanted to go with him?

261
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:25,216
Yeah.

262
00:15:29,429 --> 00:15:31,556
Look, Wen.

263
00:15:31,973 --> 00:15:34,600
Here. A surprise for you!

264
00:15:36,018 --> 00:15:38,229
I photoshopped it
with the photos you sent me.

265
00:15:38,354 --> 00:15:39,605
How's that?

266
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:43,151
- Is it good?
- Thank you.

267
00:15:46,571 --> 00:15:48,406
If you want to go
somewhere else, just tell me.

268
00:15:48,573 --> 00:15:50,533
I'll photoshop it for you.
[chuckles]

269
00:15:56,956 --> 00:15:58,916
CHANG XIN WINS

270
00:15:59,041 --> 00:16:01,543
[host] <i>After weeks of fierce
competition, the gourmet
empire, Chang Xin,</i>

271
00:16:01,544 --> 00:16:05,590
<i>has defeated
their rivals all the way
to the semifinals today</i>

272
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:07,425
<i>with unstoppable momentum.</i>

273
00:16:09,469 --> 00:16:11,387
Looks like we can't avoid them.

274
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:15,515
<i>Here we go.
Today's theme is bite-sized
Taiwanese cuisine.</i>

275
00:16:15,516 --> 00:16:19,979
<i>The Chang Xin duo is putting
on a textbook performance.</i>

276
00:16:20,104 --> 00:16:21,481
I haven't got
the vodka you want.

277
00:16:21,606 --> 00:16:24,108
It's alright.
Watch the competition.

278
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:26,360
[host] <i>Every single slice
is cut to the exact same
thickness.</i>

279
00:16:26,527 --> 00:16:28,112
[Feng] Look at how they work
together seamlessly,

280
00:16:28,237 --> 00:16:30,490
flowing smoothly
and complementing each other.

281
00:16:30,615 --> 00:16:33,116
That takes endless practice.

282
00:16:33,117 --> 00:16:36,369
[host] <i>In their hands,
every dish becomes
a work of art.</i>

283
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:38,289
[Lu-yung] They're good at mixing
different kinds of spices.

284
00:16:38,414 --> 00:16:41,125
We can enhance the aroma
through drying and extraction.

285
00:16:42,210 --> 00:16:44,337
[Feng] That Annie girl
is good-looking.

286
00:16:44,504 --> 00:16:46,631
- Very pretty.
- She's hot.

287
00:16:47,048 --> 00:16:48,132
Hot?

288
00:16:48,257 --> 00:16:49,634
Hot? Very hot?

289
00:16:51,219 --> 00:16:53,220
Not as hot as you.

290
00:16:53,221 --> 00:16:54,597
Can you focus?

291
00:16:55,306 --> 00:16:57,307
You're dead, idiot.

292
00:16:57,308 --> 00:17:00,478
[host] <i>Chang Xin
is undoubtedly the leader
in Taiwanese cuisine.</i>

293
00:17:00,645 --> 00:17:03,314
<i>They've showcased
their obsession with detail.</i>

294
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:05,191
The braised pork!

295
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:10,154
[clicks tongue] Ah!

296
00:17:11,614 --> 00:17:14,492
[host] <i>The winner
of this round is...</i>

297
00:17:14,617 --> 00:17:15,701
<i>Chang Xin!</i>

298
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:18,245
<i>Congratulations!
Chang Xin wins.</i>

299
00:17:18,246 --> 00:17:20,330
It's a no-brainer
that they'd win.

300
00:17:20,331 --> 00:17:22,290
They're skillful and creative.

301
00:17:22,291 --> 00:17:24,627
Listen to me.
They're really hard to beat.

302
00:17:28,339 --> 00:17:29,507
Go for it.

303
00:17:30,633 --> 00:17:32,051
You can do it.

304
00:17:33,177 --> 00:17:35,179
[Feng] Not easy.

305
00:17:35,304 --> 00:17:38,515
[narrator] <i>Yeah! Congratulations
to Chang Xin for blasting
their way into the finals.</i>

306
00:17:38,516 --> 00:17:41,519
<i>In our live show next week,
they'll fight
against Jin Lai Hao</i>

307
00:17:41,644 --> 00:17:43,562
<i>for the title
of King of Taiwanese Cuisine.</i>

308
00:17:43,563 --> 00:17:47,232
<i>The competition
for Favorite Female Chef
is also fierce.</i>

309
00:17:47,233 --> 00:17:49,360
<i>Ma Yu-li, the rising star
from Jin Lai Hao Food Truck,</i>

310
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:52,529
<i>has become popular
since she opened up
about being bullied.</i>

311
00:17:52,530 --> 00:17:57,242
<i>But just two days ago,
Annie Lo from Chang Xin
overtook her.</i>

312
00:17:57,243 --> 00:18:00,538
<i>An article disclosed
her hidden past, touching
the hearts of everyone.</i>

313
00:18:00,663 --> 00:18:03,082
<i>She won over many fans
overnight.</i>

314
00:18:03,207 --> 00:18:05,375
<i>This plot twist
is unbelievable.</i>

315
00:18:05,376 --> 00:18:08,169
<i>Who is going to be
our Favorite Female Chef</i>

316
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:10,171
<i>and bear the weight
of our expectations?</i>

317
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:15,260
<i>We'll find out next week.
Let's wait and see.</i>

318
00:18:15,261 --> 00:18:17,513
Can you tell me
what is going on here?

319
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:20,224
"Born and raised in a shantytown
in the Philippines,

320
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:25,062
the culinary queen of Chang Xin
has been fighting to realize
her dreams."

321
00:18:25,187 --> 00:18:27,648
You just disclosed
my private life
without talking to me.

322
00:18:28,691 --> 00:18:30,400
[Chien-yuan] <i>Hsiu-wen?</i>

323
00:18:30,401 --> 00:18:35,323
Has anything bad
ever happened to Annie before?

324
00:18:37,325 --> 00:18:39,452
Anything bad?
What does that mean?

325
00:18:39,619 --> 00:18:41,621
- Look at Yu-li.
<i>- I used to get bullied.</i>

326
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:43,748
I think it's effective.

327
00:18:45,708 --> 00:18:47,418
[dramatic music playing]

328
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:49,253
Is there a misunderstanding?

329
00:18:53,549 --> 00:18:55,467
I'm sorry.

330
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:57,637
It's my fault. Maybe I didn't
coordinate things well.

331
00:18:57,762 --> 00:18:59,429
I'll look into it.

332
00:18:59,430 --> 00:19:01,431
What's done is done.
Everyone is talking about it.

333
00:19:01,432 --> 00:19:03,267
What do you plan to do about it?

334
00:19:04,393 --> 00:19:07,270
I'll ask those platforms
to take the news down

335
00:19:07,271 --> 00:19:10,315
and try to drown out
the online comments.

336
00:19:10,316 --> 00:19:11,776
Please give me some time.

337
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:15,446
What do you think my family
will think when they see this?

338
00:19:17,573 --> 00:19:18,783
I'm so sorry.

339
00:19:28,793 --> 00:19:32,213
So, it wasn't your idea?

340
00:19:36,467 --> 00:19:40,471
I know everybody
has a spot in their heart
they don't want anyone touching.

341
00:19:40,638 --> 00:19:43,808
So, without your consent,
I'd never, ever do
anything like this.

342
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:55,486
[breathes deeply]

343
00:20:00,533 --> 00:20:03,410
It's not something
to be ashamed of.

344
00:20:03,411 --> 00:20:05,621
All I need is respect.

345
00:20:06,497 --> 00:20:08,666
What's done is done.

346
00:20:08,833 --> 00:20:10,668
I'll focus on the competition.

347
00:20:13,379 --> 00:20:14,630
Thank you.

348
00:20:19,677 --> 00:20:22,596
[pensive music playing]

349
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:35,401
Today, we're here again
with our boss, Chou Lu-yung.

350
00:20:35,526 --> 00:20:37,569
Hi, guys. I'm Chou Lu-yung.

351
00:20:37,570 --> 00:20:41,698
[Yi-hsuan] Our boss's ranking
in the Favorite Chef voting
is way too low.

352
00:20:41,699 --> 00:20:43,868
I think it's because people
don't know him well enough.

353
00:20:44,285 --> 00:20:45,661
So, today I'll show you
how cool he is

354
00:20:45,870 --> 00:20:47,538
when he's cooking.

355
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:51,458
Smile.

356
00:20:51,459 --> 00:20:52,710
[laughs]

357
00:20:52,918 --> 00:20:54,794
- Say something.
- Yeah, and...

358
00:20:54,795 --> 00:20:56,505
- When you braise the pork...
- [Yi-hsuan] Smile!

359
00:20:56,630 --> 00:20:58,715
- ...you want it to...
- [Yi-hsuan]
What's going on back there?

360
00:20:58,716 --> 00:21:00,217
- [Feng] Fire!
- [Chin-nan] Boss?

361
00:21:00,342 --> 00:21:01,593
- Boss?
- [Yi-hsuan] Fire!

362
00:21:01,594 --> 00:21:02,720
It's on fire!

363
00:21:02,845 --> 00:21:05,681
[Yi-hsuan]
Calm down, Chin-nan! Water!

364
00:21:05,848 --> 00:21:07,557
- A towel? Do we have a towel?
- [Lu-yung] I'll get
a fire extinguisher.

365
00:21:07,558 --> 00:21:08,559
Use the wiper!

366
00:21:08,726 --> 00:21:09,894
[Chin-nan] A wiper!

367
00:21:10,269 --> 00:21:11,729
[Yi-hsuan] Use a wet wiper!

368
00:21:11,896 --> 00:21:13,564
[Chin-nan]
Why are the flames so big?

369
00:21:14,732 --> 00:21:16,609
[Yi-hsuan] Calm down, Chin-nan!

370
00:21:17,610 --> 00:21:18,569
[Chin-nan] Will it explode?

371
00:21:18,694 --> 00:21:20,571
Stay back! It'll explode!

372
00:21:20,696 --> 00:21:21,822
[Yu-li] No, it won't.

373
00:21:22,031 --> 00:21:23,407
[Feng]
Maybe the gas tube comes off.

374
00:21:25,576 --> 00:21:26,702
Watch out, Yu-li!

375
00:21:36,629 --> 00:21:39,757
[triumphant music playing]

376
00:22:13,624 --> 00:22:15,416
Yu-li, you're on camera.

377
00:22:15,417 --> 00:22:16,876
- Many people are watching?
- Are you still livestreaming?

378
00:22:16,877 --> 00:22:18,462
Yeah, I haven't turned it off.

379
00:22:19,630 --> 00:22:20,797
Everything's fine, guys.

380
00:22:20,798 --> 00:22:23,716
False alarm. False alarm!

381
00:22:23,717 --> 00:22:26,345
[Yi-hsuan]
Yu-li, you were amazing!

382
00:22:26,470 --> 00:22:28,638
It's fine.

383
00:22:28,639 --> 00:22:31,308
Hi! Hello!

384
00:22:31,433 --> 00:22:34,686
Do you love our performance?
This is our special show.

385
00:22:34,687 --> 00:22:36,646
Did that fire look real?

386
00:22:36,647 --> 00:22:37,857
Didn't expect it, right?

387
00:22:37,982 --> 00:22:41,693
See you later, okay? Bye!

388
00:22:41,694 --> 00:22:43,486
<i>"Yu-li is hot."</i>

389
00:22:43,487 --> 00:22:44,529
Me?

390
00:22:44,530 --> 00:22:45,865
"Firefighting goddess!"

391
00:22:45,990 --> 00:22:47,490
It's true.

392
00:22:47,491 --> 00:22:48,993
- Are you gonna be famous?
- No.

393
00:22:49,410 --> 00:22:53,664
VOTE FOR FIREFIGHTING GODDESS!

394
00:22:53,831 --> 00:22:55,958
YU-LI

395
00:22:58,502 --> 00:22:59,752
[gasps]

396
00:22:59,753 --> 00:23:00,838
It's a tie.

397
00:23:01,922 --> 00:23:04,674
Favorite Female Chef.

398
00:23:04,675 --> 00:23:07,011
I'll take a selfie
to thank my fans.

399
00:23:10,806 --> 00:23:12,558
"Cute baby"?

400
00:23:12,683 --> 00:23:14,517
"I want to eat Yu-li..."

401
00:23:14,518 --> 00:23:15,727
"Yu-li's food."

402
00:23:15,728 --> 00:23:17,813
- What the hell?
- What?

403
00:23:18,022 --> 00:23:19,898
They're disgusting.

404
00:23:19,899 --> 00:23:22,734
Watch out for their
wild fantasies.

405
00:23:22,735 --> 00:23:24,528
Don't talk to them
so intimately.

406
00:23:24,653 --> 00:23:26,614
Mind your own business.

407
00:23:31,076 --> 00:23:33,203
Mm...

408
00:23:33,829 --> 00:23:35,748
What's wrong?

409
00:23:39,543 --> 00:23:43,172
Do you care about me
having more fans than you?

410
00:23:44,715 --> 00:23:46,758
Who cares about
how many fans you have?

411
00:23:46,759 --> 00:23:48,551
I'm worried about your...

412
00:23:48,552 --> 00:23:49,929
- your...
- What?

413
00:23:50,054 --> 00:23:51,764
Tell me.

414
00:23:51,889 --> 00:23:53,599
I'm worried about...

415
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:56,894
What?

416
00:23:57,102 --> 00:24:00,606
Are you jealous? What?
You're cute!

417
00:24:00,731 --> 00:24:02,107
No, I won't.

418
00:24:03,776 --> 00:24:05,444
NO.1: ANNIE LO
NO.2: MA YU-LI

419
00:24:05,569 --> 00:24:06,528
NO.1: MA YU-LI
NO.2: ANNIE LO

420
00:24:06,737 --> 00:24:07,820
FAVORITE FEMALE CHEF

421
00:24:07,821 --> 00:24:09,406
MA YU-LI FROM JIN LAI HAO WINS

422
00:24:09,531 --> 00:24:11,533
You can't even win
the Favorite Chef award?

423
00:24:13,786 --> 00:24:15,995
What's there to be upset about?

424
00:24:15,996 --> 00:24:18,040
Those awards
are a vote for looks.

425
00:24:18,499 --> 00:24:20,959
But I'm all about
professionalism and real skills.

426
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:22,419
Don't worry.

427
00:24:22,544 --> 00:24:24,922
In the final, we'll place.

428
00:24:32,930 --> 00:24:33,973
First place?

429
00:24:34,098 --> 00:24:37,434
Or 100th place? Or last place?

430
00:24:37,559 --> 00:24:40,604
If we participate
in a competition and let others
get all the prizes,

431
00:24:40,729 --> 00:24:41,730
what's the point?

432
00:24:41,855 --> 00:24:42,940
Drop dead!

433
00:24:48,070 --> 00:24:49,279
Hey, you.

434
00:24:50,698 --> 00:24:52,116
What are you giggling at?

435
00:24:54,076 --> 00:24:56,954
In fact, I don't know
why you're so upset.

436
00:24:57,162 --> 00:25:00,957
For that popularity award,
you disclosed my past
without my consent.

437
00:25:00,958 --> 00:25:03,919
Isn't it good enough
to end up in second place?

438
00:25:04,128 --> 00:25:07,006
It's just a show.
And we've made it to the final.

439
00:25:10,509 --> 00:25:12,635
Or maybe you want
to fire me now?

440
00:25:12,636 --> 00:25:13,846
What?

441
00:25:13,971 --> 00:25:15,639
You think I won't?

442
00:25:19,852 --> 00:25:22,688
What are you worried about?
Don't worry.

443
00:25:22,813 --> 00:25:25,023
In the final, what judges
look for are good dishes,

444
00:25:25,024 --> 00:25:26,567
not good-looking people.

445
00:25:31,030 --> 00:25:35,784
If you can't give us
any constructive advice
for the final,

446
00:25:35,951 --> 00:25:38,037
we're off now.

447
00:25:38,245 --> 00:25:41,165
[dramatic music playing]

448
00:25:45,085 --> 00:25:46,628
Fine! Get out!

449
00:25:53,135 --> 00:25:55,637
[Chang Ta-chin tidbitting]

450
00:26:00,642 --> 00:26:03,687
From catching
and raising chickens
to business management,

451
00:26:03,812 --> 00:26:05,897
you have to master everything

452
00:26:05,898 --> 00:26:07,858
to be a true owner.

453
00:26:10,986 --> 00:26:13,113
Now, which one
are we going to catch?

454
00:26:13,322 --> 00:26:15,657
[chickens clucking]

455
00:26:22,748 --> 00:26:23,874
[Chang Ta-chin chuckles]

456
00:26:27,044 --> 00:26:30,339
You have to know
how to slaughter it
to be a true owner.

457
00:26:32,007 --> 00:26:33,759
Here. Hold it.

458
00:26:33,884 --> 00:26:34,885
Dad...

459
00:26:35,010 --> 00:26:36,928
Grasp its wings.

460
00:26:36,929 --> 00:26:37,930
Come on.

461
00:26:38,097 --> 00:26:39,056
What do I do?

462
00:26:39,181 --> 00:26:40,933
Hey, that's it.

463
00:26:42,726 --> 00:26:43,852
Wring its neck.

464
00:26:45,062 --> 00:26:47,939
When you do it,
don't be softhearted.

465
00:26:47,940 --> 00:26:50,901
When you're softhearted,
it'll suffer more.

466
00:26:51,026 --> 00:26:53,612
To the chicken, this is mercy.
Understand?

467
00:26:53,737 --> 00:26:54,780
Do it!

468
00:26:57,616 --> 00:26:59,034
Come on.

469
00:27:00,953 --> 00:27:02,079
[Chien-yuan grunts]

470
00:27:05,707 --> 00:27:08,085
- I really can't do it, Dad.
- You're a good-for-nothing!

471
00:27:14,299 --> 00:27:15,801
Look.

472
00:27:15,926 --> 00:27:17,761
We're at the top
of the food chain.

473
00:27:17,886 --> 00:27:19,930
Everything below us
is livestock.

474
00:27:20,055 --> 00:27:22,182
They're born
to be eaten by humans.

475
00:27:22,391 --> 00:27:26,103
You're softhearted for it?
Are you still feeling guilty?

476
00:27:27,729 --> 00:27:29,772
Are you out of your mind? Damn!

477
00:27:29,773 --> 00:27:32,818
[dramatic music playing]

478
00:27:36,947 --> 00:27:39,116
Chou Lu-yung
is like that chicken.

479
00:27:39,241 --> 00:27:41,785
That chicken has
assaulted you twice.
Isn't that enough?

480
00:27:44,246 --> 00:27:47,666
Chien-yuan, you're my son,

481
00:27:47,791 --> 00:27:49,084
Chang Xin's future successor.

482
00:27:49,251 --> 00:27:53,297
So, when you eat meat,
don't feel guilty.

483
00:27:53,672 --> 00:27:56,049
You should take it for granted.
Understand?

484
00:28:00,262 --> 00:28:02,139
Mm-hmm.

485
00:28:02,264 --> 00:28:03,807
[chuckles]

486
00:28:08,687 --> 00:28:11,732
[chicken clucking]

487
00:28:13,734 --> 00:28:14,818
[Chang Ta-chin] Take it.

488
00:28:16,069 --> 00:28:17,237
Take it!

489
00:28:24,036 --> 00:28:25,203
Wring its neck.

490
00:28:25,204 --> 00:28:27,956
[breathes heavily]

491
00:28:33,253 --> 00:28:34,338
[Chang Ta-chin] Come on!

492
00:28:36,089 --> 00:28:37,799
[music intensifies]

493
00:28:39,259 --> 00:28:41,011
Don't you want to be my son?

494
00:28:42,763 --> 00:28:44,348
- Yes, I do!
- Prove it to me then!

495
00:28:44,765 --> 00:28:47,851
- [grunts]
- Wring it! Wring it!

496
00:28:47,976 --> 00:28:49,311
Do it!

497
00:28:50,354 --> 00:28:53,022
Do it!

498
00:28:53,023 --> 00:28:54,273
[yells]

499
00:28:54,274 --> 00:28:55,943
[cracks]

500
00:29:01,323 --> 00:29:03,700
[Chieh] Mr. Chang,
sorry to keep you waiting.

501
00:29:03,825 --> 00:29:06,285
Our show is
incredibly popular now.

502
00:29:06,286 --> 00:29:10,998
Listen. It has set a new
benchmark for cooking shows.
[laughs]

503
00:29:10,999 --> 00:29:13,168
The finals next week
will undoubtedly be the climax.

504
00:29:13,335 --> 00:29:14,795
Yes, of course.

505
00:29:15,337 --> 00:29:19,882
But I'm wondering
about the finals,

506
00:29:19,883 --> 00:29:21,093
what do you think?

507
00:29:23,262 --> 00:29:25,055
What do you mean?

508
00:29:26,932 --> 00:29:29,309
Well, Chang Xin will be
the winner, right?

509
00:29:31,895 --> 00:29:34,063
[laughs]

510
00:29:34,064 --> 00:29:37,984
[Chieh] You know,
there are many variables.
It's hard to control.

511
00:29:37,985 --> 00:29:40,404
Besides,
Yu-li is really popular.

512
00:29:40,779 --> 00:29:43,073
The final results include
an audience popularity score.

513
00:29:43,240 --> 00:29:44,991
She has the upper hand now.

514
00:29:44,992 --> 00:29:47,244
Can I have a look
at her profile?

515
00:29:47,452 --> 00:29:49,371
[laughs]
But that's personal information.

516
00:29:50,956 --> 00:29:53,916
[pensive music playing]

517
00:29:53,917 --> 00:29:56,461
[laughing]

518
00:29:57,087 --> 00:29:58,921
You know,
Chang Xin has always been

519
00:29:58,922 --> 00:30:01,425
very interested in the film
and television industry.

520
00:30:01,842 --> 00:30:04,136
We were hoping for a long-term
partnership with you.

521
00:30:04,303 --> 00:30:07,389
[tense music playing]

522
00:30:10,058 --> 00:30:11,226
But...

523
00:30:12,561 --> 00:30:15,896
we really can't let out
personal information.

524
00:30:15,897 --> 00:30:17,941
I'll have a smoke
and think about it.

525
00:30:18,066 --> 00:30:19,151
Help yourself.

526
00:30:39,171 --> 00:30:42,215
[music continues]

527
00:30:46,470 --> 00:30:47,929
CONTESTANT INFORMATION

528
00:30:57,481 --> 00:30:59,608
GENDER: MALE

529
00:31:09,618 --> 00:31:12,496
[pensive music playing]

530
00:31:21,338 --> 00:31:25,257
IDENTITY CARD
MA YU-LI

531
00:31:25,258 --> 00:31:30,054
[reporter]
<i>The next piece of news
may shock many people.</i>

532
00:31:30,055 --> 00:31:32,265
<i>On a cooking show that's been
going viral lately,</i>

533
00:31:32,432 --> 00:31:35,351
<i>Favorite Female Chef winner,
Ma Yu-li,</i>

534
00:31:35,352 --> 00:31:39,063
<i>has been exposed
as biologically male,</i>

535
00:31:39,064 --> 00:31:41,190
<i>who is currently undergoing
sex reassignment surgery.</i>

536
00:31:41,191 --> 00:31:44,443
<i>So, whether she qualifies
as a female chef</i>

537
00:31:44,444 --> 00:31:46,278
<i>has sparked a controversy.</i>

538
00:31:46,279 --> 00:31:48,865
<i>On the Internet, many people
are debating the issue.</i>

539
00:31:48,990 --> 00:31:50,449
<i>But what is the truth?</i>

540
00:31:50,450 --> 00:31:54,036
<i>We have yet to hear
what Jin Lai Hao or Ma Yu-li</i>

541
00:31:54,037 --> 00:31:55,288
<i>have to say about it.</i>

542
00:31:58,125 --> 00:32:00,043
Do you have to play
these tricks?

543
00:32:00,460 --> 00:32:03,338
Hey. But I'm telling the truth.

544
00:32:03,505 --> 00:32:06,425
What people think of her,
you can't blame me.

545
00:32:06,633 --> 00:32:08,218
You're a low rascal.

546
00:32:14,516 --> 00:32:17,436
When Ma Chih-chieh was bullied
by us all back then,

547
00:32:17,561 --> 00:32:19,229
didn't you just stand by
and watch?

548
00:32:19,396 --> 00:32:22,482
[pensive music playing]

549
00:32:25,569 --> 00:32:27,445
Don't be so upset.

550
00:32:27,446 --> 00:32:31,366
I had no choice,
because the audience
needs the truth.

551
00:32:31,575 --> 00:32:34,160
Besides, I'm your superior.

552
00:32:34,161 --> 00:32:35,579
Mind your attitude.

553
00:32:35,996 --> 00:32:37,080
Okay?

554
00:32:39,082 --> 00:32:41,168
It's about time. Got to go.

555
00:32:42,419 --> 00:32:44,588
[whistling]

556
00:32:48,091 --> 00:32:50,427
[soft music playing]

557
00:32:59,686 --> 00:33:01,605
DIE SISSY

558
00:33:01,730 --> 00:33:04,316
[school bully] <i>You look like
a ladyboy. That's great.
What a beauty.</i>

559
00:33:04,441 --> 00:33:05,984
[Hsiu-wen] Ignore them.

560
00:33:12,282 --> 00:33:14,618
- [school bully] Bullseye!
- I'll kill you, you know.

561
00:33:15,035 --> 00:33:17,204
- Fought back!
- Where's the sissy?

562
00:33:18,205 --> 00:33:19,330
- What?
- Sissy!

563
00:33:19,331 --> 00:33:20,457
- Damn!
- Don't sit here.

564
00:33:20,582 --> 00:33:22,626
- You'd get AIDS.
- Yeah.

565
00:33:23,043 --> 00:33:24,126
You idiot.

566
00:33:24,127 --> 00:33:25,504
But we can step on it.

567
00:33:27,464 --> 00:33:29,424
[school bully]
Write "freaking bastard."

568
00:33:29,633 --> 00:33:30,509
So horrible!

569
00:33:30,634 --> 00:33:32,176
He's a freaking bastard.

570
00:33:32,177 --> 00:33:33,261
And then write...
draw a chrysanthemum.

571
00:33:33,470 --> 00:33:35,013
- A chrysanthemum.
- [school bully] A loose one.

572
00:33:35,138 --> 00:33:37,223
A withered one. A loose one.

573
00:33:37,224 --> 00:33:39,350
I'll draw a large one.

574
00:33:39,351 --> 00:33:41,520
[exhales, murmurs]

575
00:33:44,481 --> 00:33:48,192
[show guest] <i>Ma Yu-li, she was
still a boy in high school.</i>

576
00:33:48,193 --> 00:33:52,154
<i>The Favorite
Female Chef title
should go to a real female.</i>

577
00:33:52,155 --> 00:33:53,698
<i>This is a matter of fairness.</i>

578
00:33:53,823 --> 00:33:55,534
[reporter] <i>The gender
controversy surrounding
the female chef</i>

579
00:33:55,742 --> 00:33:57,243
<i>on the cooking show</i>

580
00:33:57,244 --> 00:33:59,411
<i>is getting
more and more heated.</i>

581
00:33:59,412 --> 00:34:03,332
<i>Some famous streamers
are also publicly
blasting the experts.</i>

582
00:34:03,333 --> 00:34:05,502
<i>Those so-called experts
are know-it-alls.</i>

583
00:34:05,710 --> 00:34:07,337
<i>...should go
to a real female.</i>

584
00:34:07,462 --> 00:34:09,589
<i>...a real female.
...a real female.</i>

585
00:34:09,798 --> 00:34:12,008
<i>Come on.
It's the 21st century.</i>

586
00:34:12,133 --> 00:34:14,010
<i>What's wrong with wanting
to be a boy or a girl?</i>

587
00:34:14,135 --> 00:34:16,012
<i>Yu-li is a pretty girl.</i>

588
00:34:16,137 --> 00:34:18,056
<i>What's her gender
got to do with this?</i>

589
00:34:18,181 --> 00:34:20,684
Her gender is controversial.
How could she
win Favorite Female Chef?

590
00:34:21,101 --> 00:34:24,062
Being transgender
doesn't harm anybody.
Why are you boycotting her?

591
00:34:24,187 --> 00:34:27,273
How will you get married?
How will you have children?

592
00:34:27,274 --> 00:34:29,359
Although I feel like
I've been cheated...

593
00:34:29,484 --> 00:34:32,362
We all have the right
to choose what kind of person
we want to be.

594
00:34:32,529 --> 00:34:35,574
So, I see myself
as a girl and I can go
to the ladies' room?

595
00:34:35,699 --> 00:34:37,367
Don't you have anyone else,
Jin Lai Hao?

596
00:34:37,534 --> 00:34:39,159
What's wrong with diversity?

597
00:34:39,160 --> 00:34:41,580
But our identity cards
state we're male or female.

598
00:34:41,788 --> 00:34:45,458
If we don't have
gender distinctions,
our society will be in a mess.

599
00:34:45,625 --> 00:34:47,376
We can't use
a dishonest person.

600
00:34:47,377 --> 00:34:49,212
Transgender people
shouldn't exist.

601
00:34:49,337 --> 00:34:50,547
Transgender people
shouldn't exist.

602
00:34:50,755 --> 00:34:52,299
Transgender people
shouldn't exist.

603
00:34:52,549 --> 00:34:54,217
HIDING YOUR IDENTITY
IS CHEATING.

604
00:34:54,342 --> 00:34:55,385
GIVE ME BACK MY VOTE.

605
00:34:55,552 --> 00:34:58,722
[phone buzzing]

606
00:35:07,689 --> 00:35:11,234
[Lu-yung] <i>Never mind, Yu-li.
Trash people talk trash.</i>

607
00:35:11,359 --> 00:35:13,277
<i>Just ignore them.</i>

608
00:35:13,278 --> 00:35:16,322
[Yi-hsuan]
<i>I've already reported
some of the hate comments.</i>

609
00:35:16,323 --> 00:35:18,407
<i>Public opinion
is still being irrational.</i>

610
00:35:18,408 --> 00:35:20,285
- [Feng] <i>But it's cooling down.</i>
- [man] <i>Who are those nobodies?</i>

611
00:35:20,410 --> 00:35:22,244
[Feng] <i>Tell them to get lost.</i>

612
00:35:22,245 --> 00:35:23,495
[Chin-nan] <i>No matter what,
you've still got me...</i>

613
00:35:23,496 --> 00:35:25,289
[Feng] <i>Those comments
are all rubbish.</i>

614
00:35:25,290 --> 00:35:27,417
- [Chin-nan] <i>I mean, us.</i>
- [Feng] <i>Don't take it to heart.</i>

615
00:35:27,584 --> 00:35:29,585
- [Chin-nan] <i>You're the best.
-</i> [Lu-yung]
<i>Get some rest now, Yu-li.</i>

616
00:35:29,586 --> 00:35:31,295
[Feng] <i>Don't let those lies
get to you.</i>

617
00:35:31,296 --> 00:35:32,589
[Lu-yung] <i>Believe in yourself.</i>

618
00:35:32,714 --> 00:35:34,465
[Chin-nan] <i>Yu-li, we'll get
through this together.</i>

619
00:35:34,466 --> 00:35:35,634
<i>You are not alone.</i>

620
00:35:35,759 --> 00:35:37,635
<i>We all support you.</i>

621
00:35:37,636 --> 00:35:39,346
[doorbell rings]

622
00:35:42,349 --> 00:35:44,225
[doorbell rings]

623
00:35:46,603 --> 00:35:49,564
[tense music playing]

624
00:36:15,340 --> 00:36:17,509
[doorbell ringing]

625
00:36:23,181 --> 00:36:26,226
[suspenseful music playing]

626
00:36:33,525 --> 00:36:36,569
[credits music playing]

627
00:36:42,784 --> 00:36:45,829
[singer singing
in foreign language]

628
00:39:32,996 --> 00:39:34,455
[music ends]
